<title>USA: Study finds Internet use improved student learning.</title>
<headline>Study finds Internet use improved student learning.</headline>
<byline>Aaron Pressman</byline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elementary school students with access to the Internet learned more than kids who lacked access, an indepedent research group concluded after conducting a comparative study in seven urban school districts.</p>
<p>&quot;This study dramatically illustrates the positive effects of online use on learning,&quot; said Michael Casserly, executive director of the Council of Great City Schools, an association of 49 large inner city public school districts which co-sponsored the study along with Scholastic Corp.</p>
</text>
